---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/sim-lab.css';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Peripheral nerve lab" subtitle="Place contacts. Choose a fascicle. Explore the tradeoff between recruitment and selectivity.">
<div class="lab-app">
  <div class="lab-toolbar"><div class="lab-presets"><span class="lab-kicker">EXPERIMENT</span><button data-preset="focus">Focused contact</button><button data-preset="cuff">Cuff pair</button><button data-preset="multi">Four contacts</button></div><div><button id="saveNerve">Save JSON</button><button id="loadNerve">Load JSON</button><input id="nerveFile" type="file" accept=".json" hidden /></div></div>
  <div class="lab-grid">
    <aside class="lab-controls">
      <h2>Stimulation</h2>
      <label>Amplitude <output id="amplitudeValue"></output><input id="amplitude" type="range" min="0" max="150" step="1" /></label>
      <label>Spread length <output id="spreadValue"></output><input id="spread" type="range" min="0.08" max="0.65" step="0.01" /></label>
      <label>Activation threshold <output id="thresholdValue"></output><input id="threshold" type="range" min="5" max="80" step="1" /></label>
      <label>Target fascicle<select id="target"><option value="0">F1 · upper left</option><option value="1">F2 · upper right</option><option value="2">F3 · lower left</option><option value="3">F4 · lower right</option></select></label>
      <h2>Selected contact</h2>
      <label>Contact<select id="contact"></select></label>
      <div class="lab-pair"><label>X (mm)<input id="contactX" type="number" min="-1.05" max="1.05" step="0.01" /></label><label>Y (mm)<input id="contactY" type="number" min="-1.05" max="1.05" step="0.01" /></label></div>
      <div class="lab-pair"><button id="addContact">Add contact</button><button id="removeContact">Remove</button></div>
      <label class="lab-check"><input id="showField" type="checkbox" checked /> Show field</label>
      <button id="nerveReset">Reset experiment</button>
      <p class="lab-note">Drag a contact to reposition it, or enter coordinates. Click a fascicle to make it the target.</p>
    </aside>
    <div class="lab-workspace">
      <div class="lab-metrics"><div><span>Target recruited</span><strong id="targetMetric">—</strong></div><div><span>Other fascicles recruited</span><strong id="offMetric">—</strong></div><div><span>Target share of recruited sites</span><strong id="purityMetric">—</strong></div></div>
      <section class="lab-viewport"><div class="lab-caption"><span>TRANSVERSE VIEW · 2 mm nerve</span><span id="contactCount"></span></div><canvas id="nerveCanvas" width="960" height="650" aria-label="Nerve cross section. Use contact coordinate fields to position electrodes."></canvas><div class="lab-legend"><span><i class="dot cyan"></i>Recruited target</span><span><i class="dot orange"></i>Recruited elsewhere</span><span><i class="dot gray"></i>Below threshold</span></div></section>
      <div class="lab-pair lab-charts"><section><h2>Recruitment by fascicle</h2><div id="fascicleBars"></div></section><section><h2>Amplitude sweep</h2><canvas id="recruitmentChart" width="520" height="230" aria-label="Target and off-target recruitment against amplitude"></canvas><button id="exportSweep">Download sweep CSV</button></section></div>
      <p id="nerveStatus" role="status" class="lab-note">Ready.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <details class="lab-method"><summary>Model assumptions & interpretation</summary><p>This is a deterministic geometry experiment, not a physiological prediction. Four circular fascicles contain 1,200 sample sites, with fixed heterogeneous thresholds. Each contact contributes amplitude × exp(−distance / spread). Contributions add with the same sign; there is no modeled return electrode. Sites recruit when that sum exceeds their threshold. Amplitude and threshold use arbitrary units. Spread and contact positions use mm.</p><p>The cuff preset places two proxy sources at the nerve surface; it does not model a physical bipolar circuit. Tissue conductivity, axon orientation, pulse width, membrane dynamics, and injury are not modeled. The sweep reuses the same sites and geometry at every amplitude. <a href="/simulations/nerve-cross-section/guide/">Experiment guide →</a></p></details>
</div>
<script type="module" src="/scripts/nerve/main.js"></script>
</Layout>
